# tally 2.3.1 R3, P22 N6 (L §5.11 A pin is a row: two pins of one cell overlap): two `law` pins in one as if
# are LOAD-OVERLAP, as two on a line are (W3). Before: the last one won (l1 3 PLN, both pinned: lines).
=== n6.tally
model w8
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "probe"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index ks = [k1, k2]
input r[k in ks]: rate
input pct: num %
input base: money PLN
def fee: num PLN = base * pct

ask f2: fee
ask l1: fee as if {law 2026-02-01, law 2026-03-01}
ask l2: fee as if {law 2026-02-01}

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  r[k1] = 2 %/year "s"
  r[k2] = 4 %/year "s"
  pct = 1 % "s"
  base = 300.00 PLN "s"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-OVERLAP pins law 2026-02-01 and law 2026-03-01 of the law date overlap at no keys (n6.tally:16)
